{"beat": 7, "name": "WHAT TO DO", "text": "This week. First, write the cycle down. Wire date, landing date, first sale, first payout, for your top products, from your own POs and settlement reports. It's a spreadsheet with dates in it, and most operators have never made one. Next, draw the wires. Every scheduled supplier payment inside the next 90 days, on a calendar, against the cash you hold and the payouts you expect. Where the line dips lowest is your own day 13 days. Then move the clocks. Split the largest wire into a deposit and a balance where the supplier allows it. That flattens the trough without touching the margin. Trim the orders the newsvendor flags as overstocked, because that cash comes back onto the calendar. Ask for terms before you ask for growth. Last, hold cash for the trough, not for the month. Fixed costs here are $31,500 a month, and the trough arrives on day 13 days. The right reserve is the trough plus a buffer for the cone's bad tail, not a round number of months.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "This", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.267}, {"word": "week.", "start": 0.325, "end": 0.778}, {"word": "First,", "start": 0.952, "end": 1.567}, {"word": "write", "start": 1.741, "end": 2.032}, {"word": "the", "start": 2.067, "end": 2.136}, {"word": "cycle", "start": 2.183, "end": 2.496}, {"word": "down.", "start": 2.543, "end": 3.007}, {"word": "Wire", "start": 3.286, "end": 3.669}, {"word": "date,", "start": 3.727, "end": 4.133}, {"word": "landing", "start": 4.249, "end": 4.609}, {"word": "date,", "start": 4.679, "end": 5.039}, {"word": "first", "start": 5.097, "end": 5.364}, {"word": "sale,", "start": 5.422, "end": 6.002}, {"word": "first", "start": 6.153, "end": 6.42}, {"word": "payout,", "start": 6.478, "end": 7.036}, {"word": "for", "start": 7.105, "end": 7.233}, {"word": "your", "start": 7.279, "end": 7.396}, {"word": "top", "start": 7.442, "end": 7.639}, {"word": "products,", "start": 7.709, "end": 8.348}, {"word": "from", "start": 8.406